    "message": "feat(admin): providers back to a flat card grid, one card per provider\n\nThe 4.39.0 Providers page was rejected, correctly. It put every provider\nbehind a collapsed category group, so reaching one meant section -> closed\ngroup -> card -> closed \"Advanced\": four levels, two shut by default, and a\npage that opened showing mostly headings. It solved \"too much scrolling\" by\nhiding things, which is a worse problem. The status dot rail was an\nabstraction you had to learn before it told you anything.\n\nThe categories are gone entirely. \"Inference platform\" versus \"Gateway\" is a\nway of thinking about the vendor landscape, not information anyone needs in\norder to paste a key, and grouping by it made finding a provider harder.\n\nWhat this restores and what it fixes. The original 240px card grid and the\noriginal status pill are back unchanged. The one structural change is the one\nthat was actually wrong before: a provider's status and its key fields were in\ntwo different places on the page. They are now the same card. Press Configure\nand the card expands across the row to hold the whole provider form; press\nDone and it collapses.\n\nRefresh models now sits on the card face next to Configure, where it can be\nreached without opening anything -- it was buried inside the expanded form.\nLocal providers show \"Test connection\" in the same slot.\n\nCrucially, the form is the WHOLE provider, which earlier iterations of this\nwork misrepresented: the multi-key pool with per-key health, add and remove,\nthe rotation policy select, proxy and base URL. Those were never broken --\nrenderField() attaches the key manager for a credential field, so they came\nalong -- but nothing in the design acknowledged that a provider is a small\nform rather than a single input, and that is why the flat-grid ideas kept\nfailing. All 35 forms cannot be open at once; that is the real constraint.\n\nAbove the grid, the search box and Only-configured toggle stay, and the count\nline now reads \"35 providers - 6 configured\".\n\nNew payload field. `provider_status[].key_count` carries the size of each key\npool, so a card face can say \"3 keys - Round robin\" without one HTTP request\nper provider on load. It cannot be derived client-side: secrets are masked to\na constant before they leave the server. The rotation label comes from the\n_ROTATION field already in the config payload.\n\nVerification. Executed in jsdom against the real 296-field payload, and this\ntime the harness checks the things the previous one excluded and therefore\ncould not have caught:\n\n  35 cards; 0 accordion groups remaining\n  107 provider fields in the document, INCLUDING all 31 _ROTATION selects\n  31 key managers present\n  Configure + Refresh models both on the card face\n  summary line reads \"3 keys - Round robin\"\n  opening a card exposes its key manager and rotation select\n  expanding the pool lists 3 keys with health and 3 Remove buttons\n  filtering to \"alibaba\" leaves 4 cards and detaches nothing\n  a filtered-out card does not stay expanded\n  7 admin views render; no uncaught script errors\n\n  ruff format / ruff check / ty: clean\n  pytest: 3313 passed, 6 failed -- the documented PowerShell installer\n  baseline, identical on unmodified main in the same shell\n\nNot done: still not rendered in a browser; no browser tooling is reachable in\nthis session. jsdom proves structure and wiring, not appearance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
